PART 2: BLOOMBERG 5-STAGE SYSTEM DESIGN QUESTION BANK\
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\
Use the 5-Stage framework for every system design problem:\
Stage 01: Clarify (Requirements & Out-of-Scope)\
Stage 02: Interactions (Client Actions & Concrete REST/gRPC APIs)\
Stage 03: Identify Data (Relational Entities, Schema, Primary Keys, Invariants)\
Stage 04: Draw Simple Design (Minimum 3-Tier: App <-> Service <-> SQL DB)\
Stage 05: Challenge & Improve (Bottlenecks, Cache Invalidation, Concurrency, Failures)\
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\
\
================================================================================\
QUESTION 1: ROOM BOOKING SYSTEM (Official Bloomberg Workshop Question)\
================================================================================\
Problem Statement:\
Design a room reservation system for a campus or corporate office where users \
can search for available meeting rooms based on filters and book or cancel rooms.\
\
Stage 01: Clarify\
- Functional Reqs: Search available rooms by building, capacity, and amenities; \
  reserve a room for a specific time window; view personal bookings; cancel a booking.\
- Non-Functional Reqs: High availability for reads; strong consistency for bookings \
  (zero double-booking allowed); latency < 50ms for search.\
- Out of Scope: Payment processing, recurring calendar invites, room access badge IoT.\
\
Stage 02: Interactions (APIs)\
- GET /rooms?building=\{b\}&min_capacity=\{c\}&facilities=\{f\}&start_time=\{t1\}&end_time=\{t2\}\
- GET /rooms/\{id\} -> Room details\
- GET /me/bookings -> List authenticated user bookings\
- POST /bookings -> Request: \{room_id, start_time, end_time\}. Returns: \{booking_id, status: CONFIRMED\}\
- DELETE /bookings/\{id\} -> Request cancellation. Returns: 204 No Content\
\
Stage 03: Data Model (PostgreSQL / Relational)\
- students / users: user_id (PK), name, email, department\
- rooms: room_id (PK), building, capacity, facilities (JSON/ARRAY), is_active\
- bookings: booking_id (PK), user_id (FK), room_id (FK), start_time (TIMESTAMP), \
  end_time (TIMESTAMP), status (Enum: PENDING, CONFIRMED, CANCELLED)\
- Domain Invariant: A room MUST NOT have overlapping active bookings:\
  EXCLUDE USING gist (room_id WITH =, tsrange(start_time, end_time) WITH &&) \
  WHERE (status = 'CONFIRMED')\
\
Stage 04: Simple Design\
- Web / Mobile App <---> Booking Service <---> PostgreSQL Database\
- Booking Service handles validation, search querying, and transaction execution.\
\
Stage 05: Challenge & Improve\
- Bottleneck: Frequent room searches create heavy read load on PostgreSQL.\
- Mitigation: Introduce Redis Cache for room metadata and static availability bitmaps.\
- Cache Invalidation: When a booking is confirmed or canceled, invalidate search cache \
  keys for that specific room and time slice (Cache-Aside pattern).\
- Race Condition / Double Booking: Two users attempt to book Room A at 2:00 PM simultaneously.\
  Use DB transaction with `SELECT ... FOR UPDATE` or PostgreSQL range exclusion constraints.\
\
\
