QUESTION 3: REAL-TIME VWAP ANALYTICS PROVIDER\
================================================================================\
Problem Statement:\
Design a Volume-Weighted Average Price (VWAP) provider ingesting real-time trade ticks \
from 100 exchanges (100K-1M symbols, 100 ticks/sec/symbol, ~20 bytes/tick). Continuous \
running computation across time windows. Serve 100K screen users via WebSocket push and \
1K enterprise users via query APIs.\
\
Stage 01: Clarify\
- Math Formula: VWAP = (Sum of Price * Volume) / (Sum of Volume) for time window T.\
- Capacity Math: 1M symbols * 100 ticks/sec = 100,000,000 ticks/sec total peak volume.\
- User Groups: 100K live UI users (low latency WebSocket push), 1K enterprise users (REST API).\
\
Stage 02: Interactions (APIs)\
- Feed Ingestion: High-speed TCP/UDP feed handlers normalizing exchange formats.\
- WebSocket Stream: `SUBSCRIBE /vwap/\{symbol\}?window=1h` -> Pushes `\{symbol, vwap, volume, timestamp\}`.\
- Enterprise Query API: GET /v1/vwap?symbol=AAPL&start_time=\{t1\}&end_time=\{t2\}\
\
Stage 03: Data Model & Invariants\
- Canonical Tick: symbol (str), price_cents (int), quantity (int), timestamp_ns (int).\
- Running Aggregate State: symbol (PK), window_start, cum_volume (int), cum_pv_cents (int).\
- VWAP Invariant: Computed on the fly via integer division `cum_pv_cents // cum_volume`.\
\
Stage 04: Simple Design\
- Exchange Feeds -> Ingestion Gateway -> Stream Processor (Flink/Kafka) -> Redis -> WebSockets/API.\
\
Stage 05: Challenge & Improve\
- Sharding Strategy: Shard streaming processors strictly by `hash(symbol) % N_partitions`. \
  Ensures all ticks for a single symbol arrive at the same stateful aggregation worker in order.\
- Fault Tolerance: Checkpoint running cumulative aggregates (`cum_pv`, `cum_vol`) to \
  changelogs (Kafka compacted topic) every 500ms. On worker crash, rebuild in < 1 second.\
- WebSocket Fan-Out: Use a Pub/Sub tier (Redis / NATS) broadcasting to stateless WebSocket edge nodes.\
\
\
