QUESTION 4: BUILD CACHE (CI/CD Acceleration)\
================================================================================\
Problem Statement:\
Bloomberg developers experience slow builds and test executions in CI/CD pipelines. \
Design an internal distributed build artifact cache to accelerate compilation and test runs.\
\
Stage 01: Clarify\
- Functional Reqs: Check if a build task's inputs have already been compiled/tested; \
  retrieve pre-built binary artifact if present; upload new artifact if cache miss.\
- Non-Functional Reqs: Cache lookup latency < 20ms; high network throughput for binary blobs; \
  deterministic artifact retrieval (cryptographic correctness).\
- Out of Scope: Executing the build compiler itself (handled by build agents).\
\
Stage 02: Interactions (APIs)\
- GET /v1/artifacts/\{hash_key\} -> Stream binary blob (200 OK) or 404 Not Found.\
- PUT /v1/artifacts/\{hash_key\} -> Upload binary artifact stream with metadata.\
\
Stage 03: Data Model & Key Invariants\
- Content-Addressed Hash: `hash_key = SHA256(source_code_files + compiler_version + flags + env_deps)`\
- Artifact Metadata Table (Metadata DB):\
  * hash_key (PK, CHAR(64)), artifact_size_bytes (BIGINT), s3_storage_uri (VARCHAR), \
    created_at (TIMESTAMP), last_accessed_at (TIMESTAMP)\
- Storage Tier: Raw binary `.o` or `.tar.gz` files stored in distributed Blob Store (Ceph / S3 / MinIO).\
\
Stage 04: Simple Design\
- Build Agent <---> Cache Service (Metadata Lookup) <---> Blob Storage (S3) + PostgreSQL DB.\
\
Stage 05: Challenge & Improve\
- Eviction Policy: LRU (Least Recently Used) paired with a TTL (e.g., evict artifacts \
  not requested for 20 days).\
- Consistent Hashing: Shard local fast NVMe SSD edge storage servers using consistent \
  hash ring with virtual nodes for multi-gigabit streaming.\
- Cache Stampede: 50 builds trigger concurrently on the exact same commit. \
  Implement single-flight / mutex locking: only 1 agent builds, the other 49 await the artifact.\
\
