QUESTION 5: WEB APP DESIGN (Sensitive Financial Information)\
================================================================================\
Problem Statement:\
Design an enterprise financial web application supporting user onboarding, password \
reset, company financial information requests, and IT help requests. Deployments must \
be independent, authenticated, auditable, and resilient.\
\
Stage 01: Clarify\
- Functional Reqs: Secure registration, authentication (MFA), password reset workflows, \
  financial company data queries, and IT ticket submission.\
- Non-Functional Reqs: Strict security (SOC2 / PCI-DSS compliance); end-to-end encryption; \
  zero-downtime blue/green deployments; full immutable audit logging.\
\
Stage 02: Interactions (APIs)\
- POST /auth/login -> \{email, password_hash, mfa_token\} -> Returns JWT / session cookie.\
- POST /auth/password-reset/request -> Trigger signed time-limited reset email.\
- GET /api/v1/companies/\{id\}/financials -> Sensitive financial filings (requires RBAC check).\
- POST /api/v1/support/tickets -> Submit encrypted IT ticket.\
\
Stage 03: Data Model\
- users: user_id (PK), email (UNIQUE), password_hash (Argon2), role_id (FK), mfa_secret\
- roles_permissions: role_id, permission_enum (e.g., READ_FINANCIALS, MANAGE_USERS)\
- audit_log (Append-Only): log_id (PK), timestamp, user_id, action, resource_id, ip_address, signature\
- Database Choice: PostgreSQL with Row-Level Security (RLS) and column-level encryption for PII.\
\
Stage 04: Simple Design\
- Client Browser <-> API Gateway / WAF <-> App Backend Service <-> PostgreSQL Database.\
\
Stage 05: Challenge & Improve\
- Zero-Downtime Blue/Green Deployments: Deploy duplicate Green environment; run smoke tests; \
  shift traffic at load balancer level; roll back immediately on error rate spike.\
- Token Revocation / Logout: Use short-lived JWTs (15 min) + Redis distributed blocklist for logout.\
- Defense in Depth: API Gateway rate limits password-reset endpoints to prevent brute-force attacks.\
\
