QUESTION 6: KAFKA / DISTRIBUTED LOG DESIGN\
================================================================================\
Problem Statement:\
Design a distributed message streaming broker system (Kafka-like architecture) covering \
producers, consumers, partitions, brokers, message ordering, and replication under network splits.\
\
Stage 01: Clarify\
- Functional Reqs: Publish messages to topics; consume messages from topics starting at \
  an offset; maintain strict FIFO ordering within each partition; support consumer groups.\
- Non-Functional Reqs: Append-only disk write speeds; fault-tolerant replication (tolerating N-1 broker failures).\
\
Stage 02: Interactions (APIs)\
- Producer SDK: `send(topic, key, value, acks)`\
- Consumer SDK: `poll(timeout)`, `commit(offset)`\
- Broker RPC: `AppendEntries(topic, partition, messages)`, `Fetch(topic, partition, offset, max_bytes)`\
\
Stage 03: Data Model & Storage Engine\
- On-Disk Storage Format: Append-only commit log files (e.g., `0000000000.log`) segmented at 1GB.\
- Index File (`0000000000.index`): Memory-mapped sparse index mapping logical offset -> physical byte offset.\
- Message Record: offset (INT64), timestamp (INT64), key_bytes, value_bytes, crc32.\
\
Stage 04: Simple Design\
- Producer -> Broker Leader (Append-only write to active segment) -> Consumer reads via offset.\
\
Stage 05: Challenge & Improve\
- Message Ordering Guarantee: Strict ordering is guaranteed ONLY per partition. \
  Producers hash message keys to assign partitions: `partition = hash(key) % num_partitions`.\
- Network Failures & Misrouted Messages: If Producer 1 tries to send to Broker 2 due to network error, \
  Broker 1 rejects it with `NOT_LEADER_OR_FOLLOWER`. Producer metadata refreshes cluster state.\
- Durability vs. Availability (CAP Trade-off):\
  * `acks=all`: Leader waits for In-Sync Replicas (ISR) to commit before acknowledging.\
  * Quorum math: Min-ISR = 2 with replication factor 3 prevents split-brain during partitions.\
\
\
